# Machine-readable upstream review baseline. Sourced by Makefile.
UPSTREAM_REPOSITORY=https://github.com/oscardvs/zoteus.git
FORK_REPOSITORY=https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/zoteus.git
UPSTREAM_BRANCH=main
# The reviewed SHA is `main`'s TIP, not the v1.13.0 tag (`8f16efe`), which sits three
# commits earlier — the #43 dtype work, filed under `[Unreleased]` in upstream's own
# changelog, plus a registry-description fix. The tip is pinned because `upstream-status`
# compares the reviewed SHA against `main`: a tag pin leaves that target red on the day it
# is written, and a permanently-red status target is a retired one. The VERSION below
# therefore names the last release CONTAINED in the reviewed tree, which is what the
# standing page dates itself by — the gap is disclosed here and on the page rather than
# spelled into the version string, because `check_progress.PAGE_VERSION` parses `vN.N.N`
# and a `v1.13.0+3` would not match itself. Ticket 0618.
UPSTREAM_REVIEWED_SHA=b0e0bc872b5727d21ea83aba8bfe834293013264
UPSTREAM_REVIEWED_VERSION=v1.13.0
UPSTREAM_REVIEWED_DATE=2026-09-03
# The index schema generation the bench drivers target: upstream's `SCHEMA_VERSION` in
# `src/features/search/sqlite-index.ts`, mirrored in `bench/index_schema.mjs` and stamped
# into the current-generation fixture by `bench/fixtures/make_index_fixture.mjs`. It was 1
# from v1.7.0 to v1.12.0 and moved to 2 in v1.13.0, when keeping diacritics in the keyword
# index changed the FTS tokenizer and added the `accent_variants` table. That bump is the
# first this line has ever recorded, and it arrived while the leg of
# `tests/test_index_schema_fixtures.py` that compares this declaration against upstream's
# own constant was SKIPPING for want of a `fork/` checkout — see ticket 0620.
UPSTREAM_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION=2
